/* 4. k_multipass_seq: the design proposal of REPORT.md for custom waveforms, written out so the
 *    host test can run it. NOT panel data and not a proposal for wire values: every byte is an
 *    existing escape. One sequence serves every pass; what differs per pass comes from that
 *    pass's 0xAF slot, laid out as a 7-byte prefix read by SUBST plus the 800-byte register-0x20
 *    image streamed by LUT_SLICE(7, 800) to each chip:
 *      prefix[0] = PLL (register 0x30), prefix[1] = PSR byte B (0x69 OTP waveform, 0xE9 register
 *      0x20), prefix[2..6] = 0.
 *    Order per pass, as the lab drove it: stock init, PLL, PSR, 0x20 on both chips, CCSET, DTM
 *    halves, PON / DRF / POF. No TSC read anywhere: on this controller a 0x40 read reloads 0x20.
 *    It needs a slot of 807 B, which today's OD_EPD_LUT_BYTES (535) refuses. */
